    "text": "<p>We can include as many print statements in our program as we want. The expression inside the parentheses does not have to be a <code>String</code>; it can be the name of a variable, an arithmetic expression, a method call, and many other things. The expression will be evaluated and its value will be printed.</p>\n\n<p><iframe height=\"600px\" scrolling=\"yes\" src=\"https://tech.io/playground-widget/15f5cbab1beddd0d592b54ccb67990e820785/welcome/1090942/Printing%20is%20fun\" width=\"100%\"></iframe></p>\n\n<h3><span style=\"color: #cc0000;\">Do Now! </span>Assume that this code is saved in a file called PrintingIsFun.java. Run the appropriate <code>javac</code> and <code>java</code> commands to run the program. Select all of the options below that appear as part of the output.</h3>\n\n<p>(Hint: consider each option as a sequence of characters that must appear together in the output to be part of it.)</p>",
